          <CaseStudyFullImage src="/images/work/goal/interactive-map.png" alt="GOAL Global map" />
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- The Longer Relationship (signature section 2) -->
      <div class="border-t border-n200 pt-12 pb-12 lg:pt-16 lg:pb-16">
        <CaseStudySectionIntro
          label="The Longer Relationship"
          heading="One project became ten years of creative work."
          paragraphs={[
            "The website was the beginning of a sustained creative partnership with GOAL that extended well beyond the original brief. Over the following years I continued to support the organisation across a wide range of design and production work.",
            "The GOAL Next Gen department became a recurring creative relationship — producing St. Patrick's Day campaign materials for social and live events throughout the festival period. In 2024 I designed infographics for GOAL's annual report. In 2025 I designed the full Annual Report — one of the last major projects before CEO Siobhán Walsh's departure.",
            "One of the most distinct pieces of work from this period was the design of a Multi-MUAC tape — a diagnostic tool used in the field to assess malnutrition in both children and adults. Designing something that would be physically used by aid workers in crisis environments, where clarity and accuracy are not a design preference but a life-critical requirement, was one of the most meaningful briefs I've worked on. Additional work included social campaigns, event materials, and a 2-metre high jigsaw foamboard for the Irish Consortium on Gender Based Violence.",
          ]}
        />
        <div class="mt-8 lg:mt-10">
          <CaseStudyImageGrid
            images={[
              { src: "/images/work/goal/goal-jigsaw.jpg", alt: "GOAL projects" },
              { src: "/images/work/goal/goal-pday-social.png", alt: "GOAL projects" },
            ]}
          />
        </div>
        <div class="mt-8 lg:mt-10">
          <CaseStudyFullImage src="/images/work/goal/goal-muac.png" alt="GOAL MUAC" fit="contain" />
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Outcomes -->
      <div class="border-t border-n200 pt-12 pb-12 lg:pt-16 lg:pb-16">
        <CaseStudySectionIntro label="Outcomes" heading="A platform that held up — and a relationship that kept growing." />
        <div class="mt-8 lg:mt-10">
          <CaseStudyPillarGrid
            cols={2}
            items={[
              {
                num: "001",
                title: "Ten-year creative partnership",
                body: "The original website brief led to over a decade of continued creative and digital support for GOAL — across digital, print, event, and field materials. That kind of relationship doesn't happen without consistent delivery.",
              },
              {
                num: "002",
                title: "A donation platform built for conversion",
                body: "The stepped donation flow replaced a legacy system and was designed specifically to reduce friction for both one-time and monthly donors — supporting GOAL's full range of fundraising campaigns from a single platform.",
              },
              {
                num: "003",
                title: "Editorial independence for the comms team",
                body: "The campaign page framework gave GOAL's communications and fundraising teams the ability to build and publish campaign pages independently — without requiring developer involvement at every turn.",
              },
              {
                num: "004",
                title: "Infrastructure that scaled with the organisation",
                body: "Post-launch enhancements — the COVID-19 impact globe, careers API, and advanced search — were all absorbed into the existing platform without a rebuild. The architecture held.",
              },
              {
                quote: true,
                title: "GOAL Global",
                body: "Our experience partnering with Big Dog has been extremely positive. For each project, our requirements were delivered in full. Big Dog had all the skill-sets required from excellent designers to a very talented technical team to implement our projects. We look forward to engaging with Big Dog again in the future.",
              },
              {
                num: "006",
                title: "Field-deployed design",
                body: "The Multi-MUAC tape was produced for active use in humanitarian field operations — a brief where design precision had direct, real-world consequences.",
              },
            ]}
          />
        </div>
        <div class="mt-8 lg:mt-10">
          <CaseStudyFullImage src="/images/work/goal/closing.jpg" alt="GOAL Global" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </section>

  <CaseStudyNextProject
    title="Cotone"
    href="/work/cotone"
    description="Launching an Irish luxury sleepwear brand from scratch — photography, brand alignment, and a bespoke e-commerce platform built to sell."
    previewImage="/images/work/cotone/cotone-collection-preview.jpg"
  />
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  // Scroll reveal: fade + rise each [data-reveal] element as it enters view.
  // Hidden state is scoped to `.reveal-ready` (added to <html>) so no-JS shows all.
  const root = document.documentElement;
  const els = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>("[data-reveal]"));
  const reduce = window.matchMedia("(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)").matches;

  if (els.length) {
    root.classList.add("reveal-ready");
    if (reduce || !("IntersectionObserver" in window)) {
      els.forEach((el) => el.classList.add("is-revealed"));
    } else {
      const io = new IntersectionObserver(
        (entries, obs) => {
          entries.forEach((entry) => {
            if (entry.isIntersecting) {
              entry.target.classList.add("is-revealed");
              obs.unobserve(entry.target);
            }
          });
        },
        { rootMargin: "0px 0px -10% 0px", threshold: 0.1 }
      );
      els.forEach((el) => {
        // Reveal immediately if the element is already on-screen when this
        // runs (fixes inner-page heroes staying at opacity:0 until the user
        // scrolls — IO's initial callback wasn't landing reliably before
        // any scroll event; fixed July 14 2026 across all pages using this
        // script). Only observe elements that still need to come into view.
        const rect = el.getBoundingClientRect();
        const alreadyInView = rect.top < window.innerHeight && rect.bottom > 0;
        if (alreadyInView) {
          el.classList.add("is-revealed");
        } else {
          io.observe(el);
        }
      });
    }
  }
</script>
